From 945285c73b2d78fe8b8936116a3081349b4a9141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dcasati <dcasati@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:01:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] ath12k.4: add manual page

Document the LinuxKPI-based ath12k driver for the Qualcomm WCN7850:
loading, firmware files, the ath12k_wifi7N device name, the
hw.ath12k.country and LinuxKPI module parameter tunables, the tested
station-mode capabilities and the current limits.  List ath12k in
linuxkpi_wlan.4.

Like ath10k.4, the page is not yet hooked up in man4/Makefile, as the
module is not built from sys/modules/Makefile.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 share/man/man4/ath12k.4        | 214 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 share/man/man4/linuxkpi_wlan.4 |   4 +-
 2 files changed, 217 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 share/man/man4/ath12k.4

diff --git a/share/man/man4/ath12k.4 b/share/man/man4/ath12k.4
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..18b90323e34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/share/man/man4/ath12k.4
@@ -0,0 +1,214 @@
+.\"
+.\" Copyright (c) 2026 dcasati
+.\"
+.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
+.\"
+.Dd October 26, 2026
+.Dt ATH12K 4
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm ath12k
+.Nd Qualcomm IEEE 802.11be wireless network driver
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+The driver will auto-load without any user interaction using
+.Xr devmatch 8
+if enabled in
+.Xr rc.conf 5 .
+.Pp
+Only if auto-loading is explicitly disabled, place the following
+lines in
+.Xr rc.conf 5
+to manually load the driver as a module at boot time:
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+kld_list="${kld_list} if_ath12k"
+.Ed
+.Pp
+Alternatively, place the following line in
+.Xr loader.conf 5 :
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+if_ath12k_load="YES"
+.Ed
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+driver provides support for Qualcomm WCN7850 based wireless
+network devices.
+.Nm
+is derived from Qualcomm's Linux ath12k driver.
+.Pp
+This driver requires firmware to be loaded before it will work.
+The driver reads the raw firmware images through
+.Xr firmware 9
+from
+.Pa /boot/firmware/ath12k/WCN7850/hw2.0/ .
+Otherwise no
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface can be created using
+.Xr ifconfig 8 .
+The following files are used:
+.Bl -tag -width "firmware-2.bin" -offset indent
+.It Pa amss.bin
+Main firmware image, downloaded over MHI.
+.It Pa m3.bin
+M3 co-processor firmware image.
+.It Pa board-2.bin
+Board data file containing the board-specific calibration data.
+.Pa board.bin
+is used if
+.Pa board-2.bin
+is not present.
+.It Pa firmware-2.bin
+Optional container for the firmware images.
+If present, the
+.Pa amss.bin
+and
+.Pa m3.bin
+images embedded in it are used.
+.It Pa regdb.bin
+Optional regulatory database.
+.El
+.Pp
+The driver uses the
+.Xr linuxkpi_wlan 4
+and
+.Xr linuxkpi 4
+compat framework to bridge between the Linux and
+native
+.Fx
+driver code as well as to the native
+.Xr net80211 4
+wireless stack.
+The MHI bus and the QMI messaging support needed by
+.Nm
+are implemented in
+.Xr linuxkpi 4 .
+.Pp
+The PCI device attaches as
+.Li ath12k_wifi7 Ns Ar N .
+A
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface in station mode is created with:
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+ifconfig wlan0 create wlandev ath12k_wifi70
+.Ed
+.Pp
+Only station mode is supported.
+WPA2-PSK has been tested using
+.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 .
+The following operation has been tested:
+.Pp
+.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
+.It
+2.4 GHz channels at 20 MHz bandwidth.
+.It
+5 GHz channels at 20 MHz, 40 MHz (HT40) and 80 MHz (VHT80) bandwidth.
+.El
+.Pp
+The driver applies strict regulatory rules.
+Channels which the regulatory domain marks as
+.Dq no initiating radiation
+or as requiring DFS are scanned passively only.
+The regulatory country cannot be changed at runtime;
+see
+.Va hw.ath12k.country
+below.
+.Sh HARDWARE
+The
+.Nm
+driver supports PCIe devices with the following chipsets:
+.Pp
+.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
+.It
+Qualcomm WCN7850 hw2.0 (PCI ID 0x17cb:0x1107)
+.El
+.Pp
+The driver also matches the Qualcomm QCN9274 and QCC2072 PCI IDs,
+but only WCN7850 has been tested on
+.Fx .
+.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
+Tunables can be set in
+.Xr loader.conf 5
+and are read when the module is loaded.
+.Bl -tag -width indent
+.It Va hw.ath12k.country
+ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, in upper case, for example
+.Ql CA .
+The driver requests this regulatory country from the firmware before
+the boot-time regulatory domain is published.
+If unset or not two upper case letters, the regulatory domain
+reported by the firmware is used.
+The default is unset.
+.It Va compat.linuxkpi.ath12k_core_debug_mask
+Bitmask of driver debug messages to enable.
+This is also a read-write
+.Xr sysctl 8
+variable.
+The default is 0.
+.It Va compat.linuxkpi.ath12k_core_ftm_mode
+Boot the firmware in factory test mode.
+This is not intended for normal operation.
+The default is 0.
+.El
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr linuxkpi 4 ,
+.Xr linuxkpi_wlan 4 ,
+.Xr net80211 4 ,
+.Xr wlan 4 ,
+.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
+.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
+.Xr networking 7 ,
+.Xr devmatch 8 ,
+.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
+.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 ,
+.Xr firmware 9
+.Sh HISTORY
+.\" XXX Review: confirm the release before committing upstream.
+The
+.Nm
+driver first appeared in
+.Fx 16.0 .
+.Sh CAVEATS
+Do not load the
+.Pa ath12k_wcn7850_fw
+firmware module in addition to the raw firmware images.
+.Xr devmatch 8
+loads
+.Nm
+early and the firmware module then fails with
+.Dq firmware_register: ... already registered .
+.Pp
+Messages such as
+.Dq kldload: ... Unsupported file layout
+at attach time are harmless.
+.Xr firmware 9
+probes each raw firmware image as a kernel module before reading
+the file.
+.Pp
+The
+.Va wlans_ Ns Ar parent
+variable in
+.Xr rc.conf 5
+does not accept parent device names containing an underscore,
+so the
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface for
+.Li ath12k_wifi70
+has to be created explicitly with
+.Xr ifconfig 8 .
+.Sh BUGS
+While
+.Nm
+supports 802.11a/b/g/n/ac/ax/be modes,
+the compatibility code currently only supports 802.11a/b/g/n/ac modes.
+Operation in 802.11ax (HE) and 802.11be (EHT) modes, multi-link operation
+(MLO), 160 MHz channels and the 6 GHz band are not supported.
+.Pp
+Host AP mode is not supported and monitor mode has not been tested.
+.Pp
+Unloading the driver while a
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface is associated can hang the system.
+Destroy the
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface before unloading
+.Nm .
